<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TML year headline EPS rises seven pct.</title>
<headline>TML year headline EPS rises seven pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		275	   vs 258</p>
<p>    - attrib		  586	   vs 247</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 130	   vs 113</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share on a range of 302 to 304 cents, with the consensus figure at 303 cents. The dividend was seen at 132 to 135 cents with the consensus at 133.5 cents.  </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   137.1	 vs 57.3</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   169.4	 vs 82.3</p>
<p>    Tax			 33.0	  vs 24.2</p>
<p>    Operating profit	82.5	  vs 74.7</p>
<p>    Interest, investment  15.3	  vs 15.7</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	71.6	  vs 8.1 charge</p>
<p>    Turnover		  605.3	 vs 530.6</p>
<p>Div payable July 18</p>
<p>on register July 4</p>
<p>Full name: Times Media Ltd  </p>
<p>NOTE - Exceptionals mainly reflect the 80.4 million rand profit arising from the sale of 50 percent of Business Day and Financial Mail.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
